TELOMERE-CCC2-1:{"chunk":"c09","format":"ccc2-wire/1","records":[{"buys":"M minus its central line is connected — the flip binds the two sides, which is the functional equation read topologically","checksum":"0b431f84eb3e1b2de2f56b98ccf7267fded481f18cf7ad37aaeb60d291bd6dc5","id":"B1","limits":"heuristic reflection only; no operator lives on M yet","type":"B","x":"the s ~ 1-sbar flip on the Mobius band","y":"the functional equation as inseparability (sigma<1/2 cannot be separated from sigma>1/2)"},{"checksum":"86f0f564d47a0510d1d443bd4806f27480381c2e470f5dd55879e8dea3d6380d","id":"C1","kind":"definition","label":"Frobenius-like operator checklist (from the 10d template): (R1) spectrum = zeros; (R2) trace formula = explicit formula; (R3) positivity/self-adjointness <=> RH; (R4) positivity is counting-born (deg>=0 analogue); (R5) finite exact formula; (R6) stage where the s~1-sbar symmetry is geometric","note":"stipulated requirement list, fully stated in the text. Reference: the FF Jacobian satisfies R1-R6 — the template itself. BK xp: R1 shape-only, R2 smooth-only, R3 conjectural, R4 absent. Mobius band M: R6 exact, R1-R5 absent (stage, not operator). Connes adele-class space: R2 full, R1 as missing spectrum (absorption), R3 as Weil-positivity (analytic), R4 not counting-born in the deg>=0 sense. Face-complex Delta operators: R4 present, R1-R3 absent, R5 windowed only.","status":"exact","type":"C"},{"checksum":"bc3e57458bde9b4de593d9c072cc503fed8666ffce69e7bda192ea4392d73c38","generates":[{"prescription":"compute the Berry-Keating semiclassical counting function N(T) ~ (T/2pi)(log(T/2pi)-1) + 7/8","stage":"predict"},{"prescription":"|S(T)| <= 1.164, mean 0.502, drift slope 5.5e-6 — no drift","stage":"compare against 400 zeros (gamma <= 679.7)"}],"honest_boundary":"xp gives R1's SHAPE (reality of spectrum conjectured) and the smooth part of R2 only; the fluctuation S(T) — the actual zero positions — is exactly what xp does NOT give (it is the periodic-orbit/prime side, cf. the user's diagonal-approximation verification). No rigorous operator (domain issues), no R4 — sharpest spectral candidate, still a candidate.","honest_label":"conjectural","id":"D1","rule":"semiclassical N(T) ~ (T/2pi)(log(T/2pi)-1) + 7/8","subtitle":"Berry-Keating xp leg (11a)","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"BK prediction vs 400 zeros","expected":"|S(T)|<=1.164, mean 0.502, no drift"}]},{"checksum":"66ac635c16f6a7162e28df41c50c92deb186ae4a4722111e738553bdf98306a6","generates":[{"prescription":"verify |xi(1-sbar)|^2 = |xi(s)|^2 to 3.8e-16 (6 pts) — the functional equation becomes topological","stage":"descend"},{"prescription":"pairs {rho, (1-rho)bar} collapse 4->2 — CORRECTION of the earlier message: 4->2, not 4->1 (s~sbar is a separate involution; the band uses only s~1-sbar)","stage":"collapse zero orbits"},{"prescription":"images of 6 checked zeros lie on the central line sigma=1/2; RH on M: all zero-images lie on the central line","stage":"read RH on M"}],"honest_boundary":"M is a genuine STAGE (R6 exact) where the functional equation is topological; no operator lives on it yet (R1-R5 open). Figure: mobius_band.png.","honest_label":"exact","id":"D2","rule":"M = strip/(s ~ 1-sbar) with (0,t) ~ (1,-t) gluing; |xi(1-sbar)|^2 = |xi(s)|^2 descends to M","subtitle":"Mobius-band stage (11b)","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"|xi(1-sbar)|^2 = |xi(s)|^2","expected":"3.8e-16, 6 points"},{"check":"zero images on the central line","expected":"6 zeros checked"}]},{"checksum":"ec22d77a73d0c1026856ea17191f10c479e9cfb68d2537799ca6392a91a28596","generates":[{"prescription":"observe: one orientable band, 2x length, 4 half-twists (2 full twists) — the one-sidedness is destroyed","stage":"cut at the center line"},{"prescription":"Gauss linking integral of the two boundary circles: |lk| = 1.9999 -> k=4 (integrator calibrated: k=0->0, k=2->1)","stage":"verify twist count"},{"prescription":"two linked bands (thin Mobius + long 2-twist band) — the classical result","stage":"cut at 1/3 from the edge"}],"honest_boundary":"exact classical topology + computationally verified twist count; a property of the stage, not an operator result. Figure: mobius_cut.png.","honest_label":"computationally_verified","id":"D3","rule":"cutting a Mobius band along its center line does NOT give two bands: it gives ONE band, 2x length, 4 half-twists, orientable; cut at 1/3 from the edge gives TWO linked bands (thin Mobius + long 2-twist band)","subtitle":"Mobius cut topology (11d-a)","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"linking integral of boundary circles","expected":"|lk|=1.9999 -> k=4"}]},{"checksum":"b252b56e3089bbdd489ab523e7c4648ba6d7109ad0ecf12362afeb6fdfa5cf41","generates":[{"prescription":"via the orientable double cover + deck involution — m+n odd","stage":"derive the spectrum"},{"prescription":"sqrt-spectrum (0.031, 0.094, 0.157, ...) vs zeta zeros (14.13, 21.02, 25.01, ...) — no relation","stage":"compare sqrt-spectrum"},{"prescription":"the position observable |sigma-1/2| has continuous spectrum [0,1/2]","stage":"probe the position observable"}],"honest_boundary":"VERDICT negative, exact: bare geometric operators on M do not see zeros. The operator, if it exists, must see the arithmetic (prime/weight) data, not just the stage geometry. Figure: mobius_spectrum.png.","honest_label":"exact","id":"D4","rule":"truncated (|t| <= 50) Mobius-band Laplacian: lambda = (pi m)^2 + (n pi/2T)^2, m+n odd (orientable double cover + deck involution — derived, not cited)","subtitle":"Bare-stage Laplacian spectrum on M (11d-b)","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"sqrt-spectrum vs zero ordinates","expected":"no relation"}]},{"checksum":"1a7f9b853d7fd31e3d614d91378e0da005ddb2132d922313d0c85dd6e58e7895","id":"G1","result":"Bost-Connes: no zeros in the machine — gets the pole, not the zeros. Ruelle transfer: reduces to Deninger — no dynamics, no operator. Sierra xp-variants: smooth-count ceiling, same as 11a. Bender-Brody-Mueller: answer inserted by hand, not self-adjoint. Wu-Sprung: inverse tautology; the 'fractal' was approximation error.","title":"Literature operator candidates — killed (11e audit)","transfer":"CONJECTURAL-ONLY survivors: Connes 1999 adele-class (deepest reformulation; the missing Weil positivity IS RH — D10 at the highest level), Deninger program (2024 theorem proves the template dynamically only). LIVE: Connes-Consani-Moscovici zeta spectral triples (see V5).","tried":"full literature survey, 8 candidates x 8-point checklist, D1-D13 filter (operator_audit.md)","type":"G","verdict":"5 of 8 candidates KILLED by the checklist; none closes R1^R4."},{"checksum":"2fa2c7faa296c3a42bb5c4be747e5d99944ed8acc3f9155a37d17cf77eb6999d","id":"G2","result":"D1 endpoint artifacts; D2 error bars exceed resolution; D3/D4 level-count vs hidden work; D5 parallelism != complexity; D6 heuristics need bounds; D7 check the uniform null; D8 know what the medium can test; D9 name the hard core","title":"April-2026 vortex/k-reduction archive — nine guardrails","transfer":"the archive is closed archaeology; its live descendants are Circle CEIVE (our geometric language) and the honesty practice. Cross-reference before launching any filtration, heuristic-detection, or simulation-heavy step.","tried":"mined master_archive-1_0_jcc6.docx (April 2026 vortex/k-reduction factoring program) for dead ends at the user's direction -> archive_dead_ends.md","type":"G","verdict":"nine guardrails extracted; the archive itself is closed."},{"checksum":"77d7620653ccba7bdd0e888fc7898ff44375a2368d3034f2e016c6f29272cb49","from":"D3","id":"L1","rel":"supports","to":"D2","type":"L"},{"checksum":"5cedbb04636a082f665f4c3c058e421b79cb23fd1361df3c341646aa010e2f60","from":"D4","id":"L2","rel":"bounds","to":"D2","type":"L"},{"checksum":"b6f36a7cd1f31d0ee9412a587642d29f3f1b28bae2e231dd5e341b41d5abad37","from":"V5","id":"L3","rel":"implements","to":"V3","type":"L"},{"checksum":"f08d3cb915c1afdc7fc6b8196f17a9a92739be987ca9830af8abc9a2e8db5c0e","consequence":"score: sharpest sp