ONLY from Euler products over p<=lam^2; spectra numerically coincide with low zeros ('striking accuracy' even at small x); independently reproduced (Rust/MPFR, 999 digits, June 2026); authors state: proof of convergence = proof of RH (honest). Closest any literature candidate comes to our filtration language (x->infinity is a sieve-limit; Weil form on support<=S is a finite face-sum object). TOP COMPUTATIONAL TARGET: reimplement from prime Euler products alone; verify spectral coincidence; audit perturbation for zero-fitting; quantify convergence error bars (D2); map the failure mode (what spectra do if RH is false). [literature survey; primary-source abstract verified; reproduction claims secondary]","id":"V5","status":"conjectural","subject":"11e — LIVE: Connes-Consani-Moscovici zeta spectral triples (arXiv:2511.22755)","type":"V"}],"registry":{"B1":"B","C1":"C","D1":"D","D2":"D","D3":"D","D4":"D","G1":"G","G2":"G","L1":"L","L2":"L","L3":"L","V1":"V","V2":"V","V3":"V","V4":"V","V5":"V"},"wire_checksum":"35d40bb24182cb796e434d08198f173f7bdff43f9b59289c58ec52632c0ea964"}:TELOMERE-CCC2-1